message: "If you use this software or its research workflow, please cite it as follows."
title: "ClinAssist Nigeria: Calibration, Domain Adaptation and Explanation Stability Benchmark"
authors:
  - family-names: Thompson
    given-names: Ekemini
    email: ekemini.thompson@outlook.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0072-3905"
    affiliation: "Nnamdi Azikiwe University; VergelAI"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/EkeminiThompson/clinassist-nigeria"
abstract: "Research code and reproducibility workflow for evaluating calibration, controlled distribution shift, unsupervised CORAL adaptation, TreeSHAP explanation stability, and exploratory subgroup metrics on the public Pima Indians Diabetes benchmark. The benchmark is not Nigerian hospital data and does not establish clinical utility or external validation."
keywords:
  - diabetes prediction
  - calibration
  - domain adaptation
  - CORAL
  - distribution shift
  - explainable machine learning
